From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:24:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayerVideo: drop a queued drain on a flush

An end-of-data drain is queued behind the packets read ahead. A seek's
flush drops only the packets, so the drain survives and runs on the
reset decoder. A decoder that answers end of output there starts video
without its first picture.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayerVideo.cpp
@@ -0,6 +0,7 @@
 
 inline void CVideoPlayerVideo::FlushMessages()
 {
+  m_messageQueue.Flush(CDVDMsg::VIDEO_DRAIN);
   m_messageQueue.Flush();
   m_processInfo.SetLevelVQ(m_messageQueue.GetLevel());
 }
